      "guid": "de.tosox.dynamicitemweights",
      "name": "Dynamic Item Weights",
      "slug": "dynamic-item-weights",
      "teaser": "Say bye to the empty 9kg jerry can! This simple mod adjusts the weight of items based on their current usage.",
      "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/PLjwUyUmevBYgQMwXLisG0tVuMgjDLR2xXjkoYTN.png",
      "downloads": 10276,
      "favourites_count": 31,
      "description": "<h2>📜 Description</h2>\n<p><strong>Dynamic Item Weights</strong> is a mod for <em>Single Player Tarkov</em> that adjusts the weight of items based on their current usage.</p>\n<hr />\n<h2>📁 Installation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Download the latest release</li>\n<li>Copy the <code>BepInEx</code> folder into your SPT folder</li>\n<li>Start the game</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h2>📷 Preview</h2>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://github.com/Tosox/SPT-DynamicItemWeights/blob/master/readme-res/fuel_full.png?raw=true\" alt=\"\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://github.com/Tosox/SPT-DynamicItemWeights/blob/master/readme-res/fuel_used.png?raw=true\" alt=\"\" /></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>🛠️ Configuration</h2>\n<h3>In-game menu</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Enabled</strong>: Toggle dynamic item weights on/off</li>\n<li><strong>Default Tare Fraction</strong>: Fallback tare weight as a fraction of the full item weight</li>\n<li><strong>Verbose Logging</strong>: Log every single weight adjustment (troubleshooting only)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>tareweights.jsonc</h3>\n<p>A JSONC file mapping the item template ID to the tare weight in kilograms, that is, what the\nitem still weighs once it is fully used up</p>\n<pre><code>{\n    \"57513f07245977207e26a311\": 0.030, // Pack of apple juice\n    \"5d1b36a186f7742523398433\": 2.500  // Metal fuel tank\n}\n</code></pre>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If an item is missing, the plugin uses <code>Default Tare Fraction</code> of the original weight</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<h2>📄 License</h2>\n<p>Distributed under the MIT License. See <code>LICENSE</code> for more information.</p>\n",
